==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|なが|yomi=kun}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=ながい}}. First attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 712 {{CE}}.<ref>{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|長・永}}</ref> From {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|*nanka}}.

Possibly cognate with {{m|ja|流れる|tr=nagareru|t=to flow|pos=intransitive}}, and {{m|ja|流す|tr=nagasu|t=to flow|pos=transitive}}, in reference to extending.

